pe":70,"typeText":"∀ {α : Type u_1} {l l' : List.{u_1} α} (h : Eq.{u_1 + 1} l l') {i : Nat} (w : LT.lt.{0} i (List.length.{u_1} l)),\n  Eq.{u_1 + 1} (GetElem.getElem.{u_1, 0, u_1} l i w) (GetElem.getElem.{u_1, 0, u_1} l' i ⋯)","unsafe":false,"value":234,"source":{"code":"/--\nIf one has `l[i]` in an expression and `h : l = l'`,\n`rw [h]` will give a \"motive it not type correct\" error, as it cannot rewrite the\nimplicit `i < l.length` to `i < l'.length` directly. The theorem `getElem_of_eq` can be used to make\nsuch a rewrite, with `rw [getElem_of_eq h]`.\n-/\ntheorem getElem_of_eq {l l' : List α} (h : l = l') {i : Nat} (w : i < l.length) :\n    l[i] = l'[i]'(h ▸ w) := by cases h; rfl","start":270,"end":277},"axioms":[]}